WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.817
Our running project is a Student Support RAG Assistant.

00:00:03.817 --> 00:00:12.332
The knowledge base contains short documents about topics such as payment plans, internships, scholarship appeals,

00:00:12.332 --> 00:00:16.797
VPN troubleshooting, advising, registration, and graduation.

00:00:16.797 --> 00:00:26.252
A user can ask a natural-language question, and our system should retrieve the right source before generating an answer.

00:00:26.252 --> 00:00:31.402
For example, if someone asks what is required before internship registration,

00:00:31.402 --> 00:00:38.972
the system should find the internship checklist rather than guessing from general model knowledge.

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:45.198
If the question is about VPN problems, the technology support document should move to the top.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:53.397
This dataset is small enough to inspect manually, which is useful for learning.

00:00:53.397 --> 00:01:00.467
At the same time, it contains the same kinds of metadata that matter in real projects: document IDs, topics, dates,

00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:02.312
sources, and permissions.

00:01:02.312 --> 00:01:10.883
We will keep returning to the same records so you can see exactly how data moves through a RAG pipeline.
